# same tree, the first one found is tapped, and the next round reads the screen
# again because the tap changed it. A clean screen costs one read instead of
# nine; two stacked cost three, and the second is found whichever label it
# carries - the single pass this replaces could walk past it. The rounds are
# capped - a screen that keeps answering with another interstitial is news, and
# the step says so instead of looping. It stops after the sixth tap without
# reading the screen again, so it never claims to know what is on it.
